* ''The commit relay and the lead mode stay as a dev tool with a documented trust boundary'' (operator, 2026-11-04). A lead's tree counts as trusted code, and the relay's reach beyond that stands as a ruled exception to the read that found it; the broker that replaced the relay's in-memory key holds the boundary (<<~ loulou uri=`lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/seat-harness#/the-trust-model`>>).

